===== Installation Using D-Link Recovery GUI =====

  - Turn off the router.
  - Connect a Ethernet cable between one of the LAN ports on the rear of the router and the network port of your computer.
  - Configure your computer to have a static IP Address other than 192.168.0.1 (example: 192.168.0.11)
  - Press and hold the reset button on the rear of the router.
  - While holding the reset button power up the router.
  - Continue holding until the blue lights blink.
  - Open a web browser and enter the following address http://192.168.0.1
  - I have rename the factory openwrt firmware for this device to DIR1960A1_FW111B03_beta_.bin
  - Using the Choose File button select the router firmware and click upload.
  - It will then count up to 100% then display Upgrade successfully.
  - Change your computer IP Address to obtain automatically.
  - Turn off and on the router.
  - Open a web browser.
  - Access OpenWrt by typing http://192.168.1.1 on the web browser.

More information [[https://openwrt.org/docs/guide-user/installation/recovery_methods/d-link_recovery_gui|here]]
